1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,620
A dying man's last words.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,061
And they were a child's prayer.

3
00:00:04,261 --> 00:00:06,041
Jewish tradition made these words an evening

4
00:00:06,081 --> 00:00:06,401
prayer.

5
00:00:07,161 --> 00:00:08,761
Words a child could learn for the dark.

6
00:00:09,341 --> 00:00:12,322
Into thine hand I commit my spirit: thou hast

7
00:00:12,382 --> 00:00:14,482
redeemed me, O LORD God of truth.

8
00:00:14,722 --> 00:00:16,663
On the cross, the three hours of darkness have

9
00:00:16,703 --> 00:00:17,083
passed.

10
00:00:18,043 --> 00:00:20,263
With his last breath, he prays those evening

11
00:00:20,323 --> 00:00:20,663
words.

12
00:00:21,303 --> 00:00:25,104
Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit.

13
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:27,264
He begins with a word the Psalm does not have.

14
00:00:28,224 --> 00:00:28,544
Father.

15
00:00:29,505 --> 00:00:30,025
Not judge.

16
00:00:30,825 --> 00:00:31,425
Not stranger.

17
00:00:32,705 --> 00:00:33,005
Father.

18
00:00:33,205 --> 00:00:35,605
The Psalm he prayed says, thou hast redeemed

19
00:00:35,665 --> 00:00:35,965
me.

20
00:00:36,846 --> 00:00:39,106
On that cross, he was buying that redemption.

21
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:41,026
He dies like a child falling asleep in his

22
00:00:41,066 --> 00:00:41,666
father's arms.

23
00:00:41,826 --> 00:00:43,547
On the third day, morning came.

24
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:45,987
Because he rose, death loses its last word

25
00:00:46,047 --> 00:00:47,247
over everyone who is his.

26
00:00:48,347 --> 00:00:50,028
You can close your eyes in those same hands.

27
00:00:50,368 --> 00:00:51,488
Not because death is small.

28
00:00:51,908 --> 00:00:53,048
Because the hands are strong.

29
00:00:54,008 --> 00:00:56,089
Commend your spirit to the Father, tonight

30
00:00:56,549 --> 00:00:57,169
and every night.

31
00:00:58,069 --> 00:00:58,949
He keeps the morning.
